            <ArticleTitle>A nationwide perspective on asthma in older Australians.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S14-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>WHAT WE NEED TO KNOW: What is the prevalence of impaired lung function among older people in Australia? How can we differentiate between asthma and other causes of breathlessness in population-based health surveys of older people? What are the effects of ageing on people with asthma? WHAT WE NEED TO DO: Improve existing survey measures and accuracy of diagnosis. Incorporate measures of spirometric function into health surveys of representative samples of the general population. Use spirometry in the diagnostic work-up of older patients with dyspnoea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
